WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.437
Welcome to Module 5, Operational
Qualification, or OQ.

2
00:00:04.557 --> 00:00:08.611
We continue the fictional V-201 oral-
liquid vessel.

3
00:00:08.731 --> 00:00:11.803
Installation evidence identifies the
system.

4
00:00:11.923 --> 00:00:14.750
An operational test asks what that system

5
00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.629
actually does under a defined condition.

6
00:00:17.749 --> 00:00:21.818
All records and values here are invented
teaching examples,

7
00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:24.076
not approved site instructions.

8
00:00:24.696 --> 00:00:27.524
A sensor serial number supports identity.

9
00:00:27.644 --> 00:00:32.678
A controlled input and measured response
support a functional conclusion.

10
00:00:32.798 --> 00:00:36.729
Product mixing performance needs its own
justified study.

11
00:00:36.849 --> 00:00:39.884
These evidence questions can be
coordinated,

12
00:00:40.004 --> 00:00:45.245
but a successful operational test alone
does not establish blend uniformity,

13
00:00:45.365 --> 00:00:48.951
cleaning effectiveness or permission to
manufacture.

14
00:00:49.571 --> 00:00:53.295
A comfortable set point is only one part
of operation.

15
00:00:53.415 --> 00:00:57.277
Select meaningful operating conditions
from the intended

16
00:00:57.397 --> 00:00:59.397
use and system knowledge.

17
00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:02.414
A minimum level may challenge one function

18
00:01:02.534 --> 00:01:05.224
while a higher load challenges another.

19
00:01:05.344 --> 00:01:10.240
Explain why the selected conditions expose
relevant failure mechanisms,

20
00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.705
rather than treating a maximum value as
universally worst case.

21
00:01:15.325 --> 00:01:20.498
The conclusion identifies the tested
configuration, conditions and results.

22
00:01:20.618 --> 00:01:23.754
It also identifies what was not
demonstrated.

23
00:01:23.874 --> 00:01:26.839
A simulation that checks the controller
may

24
00:01:26.959 --> 00:01:30.138
leave a physical sensor or actuator
untested.

25
00:01:30.258 --> 00:01:34.534
This is a useful partial result when its
boundary is explicit,

26
00:01:34.654 --> 00:01:37.895
not evidence for an unchallenged complete
loop.
